# %SYSTEM_NAME% Module: %SYSTEM_ID%

This module is designed for the %SYSTEM_NAME% system. It includes SDK-conforming scaffolding for UI, logic, and server components.

## Directory Structure

- `module/`: Public logic, UI, and server entry points.
- `assets/`: Static assets and hand-authored stylesheets served through the module asset route.
- `src/logic/`: Implement your module's logic and data transformations here.
- `src/ui/`: Create the presentational actor sheet and other React surfaces here.
- `src/server/`: Add system-specific API routes over the request runtime here.
- `src/styles/tailwind.css`: Your Tailwind entry — see Styling below.
- `.github/workflows/`: Validation and release automation pinned to the Sheet Delver release used to create this module.

## Styling

Two paths, freely mixed (ADR-0027 section M):

- **Tailwind utility classes** in your components (`className="flex gap-2 text-2xl"`). At package time these compile from `src/styles/tailwind.css` into `assets/%SYSTEM_ID%.tailwind.css`, scoped under `.sdk-module--%SYSTEM_ID%`. In local dev the host scans your source directly, so utilities just work. Extend the entry with `@theme`, `@layer components { … @apply … }`, or `@font-face` as needed. (If your module uses no utilities at all, delete `src/styles/tailwind.css`.)
- **Hand-authored CSS** in `assets/styles.css`, declared via `stylesheet` in `module/ui.tsx`. Use semantic class names; keep selectors under `.sdk-module--%SYSTEM_ID%` (the checker enforces this).

The compiled Tailwind artifact and your declared stylesheets load as separate `<link>`s and compose via the cascade — they are never merged.

## Getting Started

1. Implement your adapter projections in the `src/logic/` directory.
2. Build your actor sheet over `ActorSheetProps` in the `src/ui/` directory.
3. Add system-specific server routes using `req.runtime` in the `src/server/` directory.
4. Run `npm run module:check %SYSTEM_ID%` before packaging.
5. Review the generated workflows and keep their Sheet Delver core ref pinned to a tested release.

## Validation And Releases

The generated validation workflow checks this module against Sheet Delver
`%CORE_REF%` on pull requests, pushes to `main`, and manual runs. It runs both
the module contract checker and a complete package build in an isolated data
directory.

The generated release workflow runs only for pushed `v*` tags. Before tagging,
set `info.json` `version` to the intended release version and commit the change.
The tag without its leading `v` must exactly match that version. For example,
module version `1.2.0` is released with tag `v1.2.0`.

The release workflow publishes the generated archive, SHA-256 checksum, and
`sheet-delver-manifest.json` as GitHub Release assets. It does not write to any
developer `local/modules` directory.

Refer to the [Sheet Delver Module Manifest documentation](https://github.com/sheetdelver/sheetdelver/blob/main/docs/MODULE_MANIFEST.md) for detailed API usage and examples.

Happy developing!
